      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Upvoting this. It is very limiting currently to not be able to do basic math between two parameters without resorting to a convoluted setup adding unnecessary complexity and lag. I'm currently working on an item with random values and I want easy access to the luck percentages for the users through parameters. However, without any way to do this kind of math easily through the Parameter Driver, I'm forced to hard code them in the animator's transitions, making it much more tedious to edit all of them. Or do that convoluted setup, which I'm not willing to do for obvious reasons.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-15T09:08:51.645Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The Avatar Parameter Driver component can add to a paramater, but cannot add two parameters together. \n\nThe only way to do this is to use an Animated Animator Parameter, which cannot be sync'd. To sync the result of this you need to use proximity contacts and sync the result. This whole system means that to do basic maths operations, you need to have multiple layers, contacts and excess parameters. In general, this is a very clunky system, which creates unnessecary lag.\n\nThe Avatar Parameter Driver can already add a fixed value to a parameter, allowing it to add two Parameters together would cause a lot less friction in these cases.",
